* PROMPT and HELP forms (OCL-07, RV-40). From SC41-4731 chapters 4 and 5.
* Each PROMPT and HELP is reported R and copied as a comment.
* Example 1: the minimum
// PROMPT MEMBER-PROMPTS,FORMAT-DISPLAY1
* LIBRARY and a length for each parameter
// PROMPT MEMBER-SCREENS,FORMAT-DISPLAY1,LIBRARY-MYLIB,LENGTH-'8,6,8,8,8'
* Example 3: parameters 6 to 10, blank lengths are 8
// PROMPT MEMBER-SCREENS,FORMAT-DISPLAY2,START-6,LENGTH-',,,20,'
* Length 0 skips a parameter, PDATA-YES, UPSI switches as indicators 91 to 98
// PROMPT MEMBER-SCREENS,FORMAT-DISPLAY3,LENGTH-'1,0,2',PDATA-YES,UPSI-YES
* Example 4: a value set before the PROMPT, then the procedure call
// EVALUATE P1=A
// PROMPT MEMBER-SCREENS,FORMAT-DISPLAY3,LENGTH-'1,2'
PROCB ?1?,?2?
* The key pressed is in ?CD?: 0000 Enter, 2001 to 2024 CF1 to CF24, 2090 to 2093
// IF ?CD?-2003 GOTO END
// IF ?CD?-2092 GOTO HLP
* PROMPT as the statement part of an IF
// IF ?1?/ PROMPT MEMBER-SCREENS,FORMAT-F1
// IF DSPLY-IGC PROMPT MEMBER-FORMATS,FORMAT-FMT1
// TAG HLP
* HELP: the User Support menu, a procedure, OCL help and PCE help
HELP
HELP LISTLIBR
HELP BLDLIBR,MYLIB
HELP OCL
HELP PCE
// TAG END
